WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.958
Let's turn a recording into a practice exercise.

00:02.958 --> 00:07.083
We'll load one file, create a drill for one line, and

00:07.083 --> 00:10.208
save the result.

00:10.208 --> 00:14.000
On the Discover page, click Start with my own recording.

00:14.000 --> 00:15.542
This opens Audio Lab.

00:15.542 --> 00:20.958
You can also reach it from the top menu.

00:20.958 --> 00:23.542
Find the section called Your recording.

00:23.542 --> 00:28.292
Under Choose local reference audio, click the file chooser and select

00:28.292 --> 00:32.917
the audio file on your computer.

00:32.917 --> 00:35.708
Its name and a player should now appear.

00:35.708 --> 00:41.208
The file stays in this tab; it is not uploaded.

00:41.208 --> 00:43.500
Press the triangular Play button.

00:43.500 --> 00:49.167
This synthetic clip demonstrates the workflow, not an accent model.

00:49.167 --> 00:52.708
Discover the joy of phonetics.

00:52.708 --> 00:57.333
Now click Use this reference in Coach.

00:57.333 --> 01:02.042
Coach Workspace opens with the filename in the recording reference field.

01:02.042 --> 01:07.917
Leave Archive sample empty; we're using our own file.

01:07.917 --> 01:12.250
In Short phrase or scene line, type Discover the joy of

01:12.250 --> 01:14.667
phonetics.

01:14.667 --> 01:20.125
Under Teaching context, give the session a name.

01:20.125 --> 01:26.792
In Teaching task, write Invite a colleague to explore the resource.

01:26.792 --> 01:30.625
In Sound target one, write Explore the J sound at the

01:30.625 --> 01:33.708
start of joy.

01:33.708 --> 01:38.458
In target two, write Move the main emphasis from JOY to

01:38.458 --> 01:40.875
PHONETICS.

01:40.875 --> 01:45.000
In target three, write Try a rising ending, then a falling

01:45.000 --> 01:45.375
ending.

01:45.375 --> 01:49.542
One target is enough for a first session; the other two

01:49.542 --> 01:52.292
are optional.

01:52.292 --> 01:53.458
Click Build drill.

01:53.458 --> 01:58.583
The draft appears in the third panel, Drill.

01:58.583 --> 02:02.667
This copies your phrase and targets into a starting structure.

02:02.667 --> 02:07.167
It has not analysed your recording.

02:07.167 --> 02:11.583
Click inside the drill text and add your own teaching directions:

02:11.583 --> 02:12.375
Listen once.

02:12.375 --> 02:14.792
Practise one feature at a time.

02:14.792 --> 02:20.458
Then say the whole line to your imagined colleague.

02:20.458 --> 02:25.208
Have the student try one choice, then return to the whole

02:25.208 --> 02:25.667
line.

02:25.667 --> 02:32.458
Choose what serves the invitation; these are not universal accent rules.

02:32.458 --> 02:35.250
Scroll down to Observations and next changes.

02:35.250 --> 02:39.667
Write what was actually heard and one question for the next

02:39.667 --> 02:42.083
lesson.

02:42.083 --> 02:47.500
Keep the teacher's comments in Expert feedback, and only with permission.

02:47.500 --> 02:54.417
This demonstration does not invent student observations or expert comments.

02:54.417 --> 02:59.667
Return to the Drill panel and click Save session.

02:59.667 --> 03:02.417
Check for Session saved in this browser.

03:02.417 --> 03:08.750
This saves notes locally in this browser, not the audio file.

03:08.750 --> 03:12.167
Your session should also appear below under Saved sessions.

03:12.167 --> 03:17.958
Use Open to return to it later in this browser.

03:17.958 --> 03:21.792
At the top of Coach Workspace, click Export session.

03:21.792 --> 03:28.042
Your browser downloads a JSON backup of the session notes.

03:28.042 --> 03:31.042
Keep this backup and the original recording separately.

03:31.042 --> 03:37.208
Audio is not included in the backup or a share link.

03:37.208 --> 03:41.833
After a reload, choose the audio file again in Audio Lab.

03:41.833 --> 03:46.417
Review your notes before sharing anything.

03:46.417 --> 03:50.917
You now have a recording reference, a clear practice task, and

03:50.917 --> 03:52.125
a saved backup.

03:52.125 --> 03:56.625
The teacher and student make the performance choices; the prototype does

03:56.625 --> 04:01.083
not give an automatic accent score.
